2026-10-31 18:06:16,971 - openai._base_client - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-1797ca90-5c96-4f97-8e28-718579f2d07c', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': '【当前系统时间】\n2026-10-31 18:06:16（周六）\n涉及日期、时间、时效性判断（如“今天”“本月”“最近”）时，一律以上述时间为基准，不得臆造、替换或推算错误的时间。当用户未提出时间内容时不要随意推算或带入当前时间。按照用户提问为准该时间只是校准用，不作为业务时间（除用户提出今天或者等等意图时才可以带入）。\n\n【主技能画像】\n- 技能ID: 36\n- 技能名称: 分析客户合同销售毛利率\n- 技能描述: 查询出所有客户相关联的合同并计算销售金额算出bom物料成本价格计算毛利率分析客户画像以及合同数量全方位分析\n\n【主技能规则口径】\n查询出所有客户相关联的合同并计算销售金额算出bom物料成本价格计算毛利率分析客户画像以及合同数量全方位分析，销售合同以erp系统为准\n\n【本次执行单元清单】\n- 技能ID: 36, 名称: 分析客户合同销售毛利率, 描述: 查询出所有客户相关联的合同并计算销售金额算出bom物料成本价格计算毛利率分析客户画像以及合同数量全方位分析\n\n【技能组全局设定】\n技能组：nova系统\nerp+crm客户与销售产线系统合并技能\n\n你是负责最终业务总结的助手。请对本次技能的执行结果做业务解读与总结。'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '用户原始问题：华信健康的订单总额是多少，订单成本及毛利率多少，以及物料详情明细给我\n\n【技能各执行单元的过程与结果】\n## 执行单元【分析客户合同销售毛利率】结果\n\n### 步骤 1: 步骤1：查询客户\'华信健康\'关联的所有销售订单及其明细，计算订单销售总额；同时通过BOM结构卷算对应产品的标准物料成本，计算总成本及毛利率，并输出涉及的物料详情明细\n**执行代码**:\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom decimal import Decimal\n\nconn = get_connection()\nif conn is None:\n    raise Exception("Database connection failed")\n\ntry:\n    cursor = conn.cursor()\n    \n    # 1. Query Sales Orders and Items for customer \'华信健康\'\n    sql_orders = """\n    SELECT \n        so.order_no,\n        so.customer_name,\n        so.total_amount AS order_total_amount,\n        soi.product_id,\n        soi.product_code,\n        soi.product_name,\n        soi.quantity,\n        soi.unit_price,\n        soi.amount AS item_amount\n    FROM nova_erp.erp_sales_order so\n    JOIN nova_erp.erp_sales_order_item soi ON so.id = soi.order_id\n    WHERE so.customer_name LIKE %s\n      AND so.is_deleted = 0\n      AND so.status IN (2,3,4,5) -- Exclude cancelled/draft if needed, but usually completed/shipped are relevant for cost analysis. Let\'s include all non-deleted to be safe or filter by status > 1. The prompt asks for "orders", usually implies valid ones. I\'ll include all non-deleted to capture full picture, but note that cancelled orders might have zero delivery.\n    """\n    # Refining status filter: Usually we analyze actual sales. Status 2-Approved, 3-Partial Ship, 4-Shipped, 5-Completed. 6-Cancelled.\n    # Let\'s stick to non-cancelled for meaningful gross margin analysis unless specified otherwise.\n    sql_orders = """\n    SELECT \n        so.order_no,\n        so.customer_name,\n        so.total_amount AS order_total_amount,\n        soi.product_id,\n        soi.product_code,\n        soi.product_name,\n        soi.quantity,\n        soi.unit_price,\n        soi.amount AS item_amount\n    FROM nova_erp.erp_sales_order so\n    JOIN nova_erp.erp_sales_order_item soi ON so.id = soi.order_id\n    WHERE so.customer_name LIKE %s\n      AND so.is_deleted = 0\n      AND so.status != 6\n    """\n    \n    cursor.execute(sql_orders, (\'%华信健康%\',))\n    rows_orders = cursor.fetchall()\n    \n    if not rows_orders:\n        print("No orders found for customer \'华信健康\'.")\n    else:\n        df_orders = pd.DataFrame(rows_orders, columns=[\'order_no\', \'customer_name\', \'order_total_amount\', \'product_id\', \'product_code\', \'product_name\', \'quantity\', \'unit_price\', \'item_amount\'])\n        \n        # Convert decimals to float for calculation\n        numeric_cols = [\'order_total_amount\', \'quantity\', \'unit_price\', \'item_amount\']\n        for col in numeric_cols:\n            df_orders[col] = df_orders[col].astype(float)\n            \n        total_sales_amount = df_orders[\'item_amount\'].sum()\n        \n        # 2. Calculate BOM Cost for each product line\n        # We need to traverse the BOM. Since SQL recursive CTEs can be complex or unsupported depending on MySQL version, \n        # and the data volume per order is likely small, we can do this in Python using a helper function or iterative queries.\n        # However, doing it row-by-row with multiple queries is slow. \n        # Better approach: Get all unique product_ids from the orders, then fetch their BOM structures.\n        \n        unique_product_ids = df_orders[\'product_id\'].unique().tolist()\n        \n        # Fetch BOM Heads for these products (Sales BOM type=3 or Manufacturing BOM type=2? \n        # Prompt says "bom物料成本价格". Usually standard cost comes from MBOM or EBOM. \n        # erp_bom.bom_type: 1-EBOM, 2-MBOM, 3-Sales BOM. \n        # Standard cost is typically derived from the production BOM (MBOM). Let\'s assume MBOM (type=2) or EBOM (type=1) if no specific instruction. \n        # Often "Cost" implies manufacturing cost. Let\'s look for published BOMs.\n        # Let\'s try to find the most recent published BOM for each material.\n        \n        sql_boms = """\n        SELECT id, material_id, bom_version, base_qty, yield_rate\n        FROM nova_erp.erp_bom\n        WHERE material_id IN ({})\n          AND status = 2 -- Published\n          AND bom_type IN (1, 2) -- Engineering or Manufacturing BOMs are used for costing\n        ORDER BY effective_date DESC\n        """.format(\',\'.join([\'%s\'] * len(unique_product_ids)))\n        \n        cursor.execute(sql_boms, unique_product_ids)\n        rows_boms = cursor.fetchall()\n        \n        # Map material_id to its best BOM head (latest published)\n        bom_head_map = {}\n        for row in rows_boms:\n            mid = row[1]\n            if mid not in bom_head_map:\n                bom_head_map[mid] = {\n                    \'id\': row[0],\n                    \'version\': row[2],\n                    \'base_qty\': float(row[3]),\n                    \'yield_rate\': float(row[4]) if row[4] else 100.0\n                }\n                \n        # If some products don\'t have a BOM, they might be purchased items directly.\n        # For purchased items, cost is often purchase price or standard cost in material master.\n        # erp_material.standard_cost\n        \n        missing_bom_products = [pid for pid in unique_product_ids if pid not in bom_head_map]\n        \n        # Fetch Standard Costs for materials (both those with BOMs - leaf nodes will use this, and those without BOMs)\n        # Actually, we need costs for ALL components in the BOM tree.\n        # Strategy:\n        # 1. Identify all component material IDs involved in the BOMs of the sold products.\n        # 2. Get their standard costs.\n        # 3. Roll up costs.\n        \n        # This is getting complex for a single script step without recursion limits.\n        # Simplified Approach for "Analysis":\n        # Assume 1-level BOM expansion first. If multi-level, we need more logic.\n        # Given the table structure supports multi-layer via self-reference in `erp_bom_item` -> `component_material_id`,\n        # let\'s try to calculate cost based on direct children first. If a child has its own BOM, we should ideally recurse.\n        # For robustness in this sandbox, I will implement a simple recursive cost calculator using cached queries.\n        \n        def get_material_standard_cost(material_id):\n            sql = "SELECT standard_cost FROM nova_erp.erp_material WHERE id = %s"\n            cursor.execute(sql, (material_id,))\n            res = cursor.fetchone()\n            return float(res[0]) if res and res[0] is not None else 0.0\n            \n        def get_bom_items(bom_id):\n            sql = """\n            SELECT component_material_id, qty_per, loss_rate\n            FROM nova_erp.erp_bom_item\n            WHERE bom_id = %s\n            """\n            cursor.execute(sql, (bom_id,))\n            return cursor.fetchall()\n            \n        # Cache for calculated unit costs of materials to avoid re-calculating sub-assemblies\n        unit_cost_cache = {}\n        \n        def calculate_unit_cost(material_id, visited=None):\n            if visited is None:\n                visited = set()\n            \n            if material_id in unit_cost_cache:\n                return unit_cost_cache[material_id]\n                \n            if material_id in visited:\n                return 0.0 # Prevent infinite loop\n                \n            visited.add(material_id)\n            \n            # Check if this material has a published BOM\n            # We already fetched bom_head_map for top-level products. \n            # But sub-components might also have BOMs. We need to check DB for any BOM associated with this material_id.\n            \n            sql_check_bom = """\n            SELECT id, base_qty, yield_rate\n            FROM nova_erp.erp_bom\n            WHERE material_id = %s AND status = 2 AND bom_type IN (1,2)\n            ORDER BY effective_date DESC LIMIT 1\n            """\n            cursor.execute(sql_check_bom, (material_id,))\n            bom_row = cursor.fetchone()\n            \n            if bom_row:\n                bom_id = bom_row[0]\n                base_qty = float(bom_row[1])\n                yield_rate = float(bom_row[2]) if bom_row[2] else 100.0\n                \n                items = get_bom_items(bom_id)\n                total_child_cost = 0.0\n                \n                for item in items:\n                    comp_mid = item[0]\n                    qty_per = float(item[1])\n                    loss_rate = float(item[2]) if item[2] else 0.0\n                    \n                    # Effective quantity needed per base unit\n                    eff_qty = qty_per * (1 + loss_rate / 100.0)\n                    \n                    child_unit_cost = calculate_unit_cost(comp_mid, visited.copy())\n                    \n                    total_child_cost += eff_qty * child_unit_cost\n                \n                # Adjust for yield rate at this level\n                # Cost per finished unit = Total Child Cost / Yield Rate\n                if yield_rate > 0:\n                    final_cost = total_child_cost / (yield_rate / 100.0)\n                else:\n                    final_cost = total_child_cost\n                    \n                unit_cost_cache[material_id] = final_cost\n                return final_cost\n            else:\n                # No BOM, it\'s a raw material/purchased part. Use standard cost.\n                std_cost = get_material_standard_cost(material_id)\n                unit_cost_cache[material_id] = std_cost\n                return std_cost\n\n        # Calculate total cost for the order lines\n        df_orders[\'unit_cost\'] = df_orders.apply(lambda row: calculate_unit_cost(row[\'product_id\']), axis=1)\n        df_orders[\'total_cost\'] = df_orders[\'quantity\'] * df_orders[\'unit_cost\']\n        \n        total_cost = df_orders[\'total_cost\'].sum()\n        \n        gross_margin = 0.0\n        if total_sales_amount > 0:\n            gross_margin = (total_sales_amount - total_cost) / total_sales_amount * 100\n            \n        # Output Summary\n        print(f"Customer: 华信健康")\n        print(f"Total Order Count: {df_orders[\'order_no\'].nunique()}")\n        print(f"Total Sales Amount: {total_sales_amount:.2f}")\n        print(f"Total Calculated Cost: {total_cost:.2f}")\n        print(f"Gross Margin: {gross_margin:.2f}%")\n        print("\\n--- Order Details & Material Cost Breakdown ---")\n        \n        # Prepare detailed output\n        # We want to show which materials contributed to the cost.\n        # To keep it readable, we\'ll list the main product lines and their calculated unit cost.\n        # For deeper detail, we could expand BOMs, but that might be too verbose.\n        # The prompt asks for "物料详情明细" (Material details).\n        # I will create a separate dataframe showing the expanded BOM components for the top-selling items or all items if few.\n        \n        # Let\'s generate a BOM explosion report for the products in the orders\n        exploded_rows = []\n        for _, row in df_orders.iterrows():\n            prod_id = row[\'product_id\']\n            prod_name = row[\'product_name\']\n            qty_sold = row[\'quantity\']\n            \n            # Find BOM for this product\n            sql_find_bom = """\n            SELECT id, base_qty, yield_rate\n            FROM nova_erp.erp_bom\n            WHERE material_id = %s AND status = 2 AND bom_type IN (1,2)\n            ORDER BY effective_date DESC LIMIT 1\n            """\n            cursor.execute(sql_find_bom, (prod_id,))\n            b = cursor.fetchone()\n            \n            if b:\n                bom_id = b[0]\n                base_qty = float(b[1])\n                yield_rate = float(b[2]) if b[2] else 100.0\n                \n                sql_items = """\n                SELECT bi.component_material_id, m.material_code, m.material_name, bi.qty_per, bi.loss_rate, m.standard_cost\n                FROM nova_erp.erp_bom_item bi\n                JOIN nova_erp.erp_material m ON bi.component_material_id = m.id\n                WHERE bi.bom_id = %s\n                """\n                cursor.execute(sql_items, (bom_id,))\n                comps = cursor.fetchall()\n                \n                for c in comps:\n                    comp_mid = c[0]\n                    comp_code = c[1]\n                    comp_name = c[2]\n                    qty_per = float(c[3])\n                    loss_rate = float(c[4]) if c[4] else 0.0\n                    std_cost = float(c[5]) if c[5] else 0.0\n                    \n                    # Calculate required qty for this sale\n                    # Qty per base unit * (1+loss) * (Sold Qty / Base Qty) / Yield?\n                    # Simplified: Effective Qty per Unit = Qty_per * (1+Loss/100)\n                    # Total Component Qty = Effective Qty per Unit * Sold Qty / (Yield/100) ? \n                    # Usually BOM quantities are relative to base_qty.\n                    # If base_qty is 1, then qty_per is per unit.\n                    # Let\'s assume base_qty normalizes the BOM.\n                    # Required per finished good = (qty_per * (1+loss_rate/100)) / (yield_rate/100) ?? \n                    # Actually, yield affects how many FG you get from inputs. \n                    # Input Qty = Output Qty * (Qty Per) * (1+Loss) / Yield.\n                    \n                    eff_qty_per_fg = (qty_per * (1 + loss_rate/100.0)) / (yield_rate/100.0) if yield_rate > 0 else 0\n                    total_comp_qty = eff_qty_per_fg * qty_sold\n                    total_comp_cost = total_comp_qty * std_cost\n                    \n                    exploded_rows.append({\n                        \'Order_No\': row[\'order_no\'],\n                        \'Product_Name\': prod_name,\n                        \'Component_Code\': comp_code,\n                        \'Component_Name\': comp_name,\n                        \'Unit_Cost\': std_cost,\n                        \'Required_Qty_Per_FG\': round(eff_qty_per_fg, 4),\n                        \'Total_Required_Qty\': round(total_comp_qty, 2),\n                        \'Total_Component_Cost\': round(total_comp_cost, 2)\n                    })\n            else:\n                # No BOM, treat as purchased/raw\n                std_c = get_material_standard_cost(prod_id)\n                exploded_rows.append({\n                    \'Order_No\': row[\'order_no\'],\n                    \'Product_Name\': prod_name,\n                    \'Component_Code\': \'N/A (Direct)\',\n                    \'Component_Name\': f"{prod_name} (Standard Cost)",\n                    \'Unit_Cost\': std_c,\n                    \'Required_Qty_Per_FG\': 1.0,\n                    \'Total_Required_Qty\': qty_sold,\n                    \'Total_Component_Cost\': round(qty_sold * std_c, 2)\n                })\n                \n        df_exploded = pd.DataFrame(exploded_rows)\n        if not df_exploded.empty:\n            print("\\n--- Material Detail Breakdown (BOM Explosion) ---")\n            print(df_exploded.to_string(index=False))\n        else:\n            print("\\nNo material details found.")\n\nfinally:\n    conn.rollback()\n    conn.close()\n```\n**执行结果**:\n```text\nCustomer: 华信健康\nTotal Order Count: 1\nTotal Sales Amount: 1126887.04\nTotal Calculated Cost: 9349.32\nGross Margin: 99.17%\n\n--- Order Details & Material Cost Breakdown ---\n\n--- Material Detail Breakdown (BOM Explosion) ---\n      Order_No   Product_Name Component_Code Component_Name  Unit_Cost  Required_Qty_Per_FG  Total_Required_Qty  Total_Component_Cost\nSO202607140001 六轴工业机器人 六轴-729         RM0002        6061铝型材      28.00               4.2449                4.24                118.86\nSO202607140001 六轴工业机器人 六轴-729         RM0007           伺服电机    1850.00               1.0204                1.02               1887.76\nSO202607140001 六轴工业机器人 六轴-729         RM0009          谐波减速机    4200.00               1.0204                1.02               4285.71\nSO202607140001 六轴工业机器人 六轴-729         RM0011          深沟球轴承      26.00               4.1633                4.16                108.24\nSO202607140001 六轴工业机器人 六轴-729         RM0005        精密内六角螺栓       0.85              12.9796               12.98                 11.03\nSO202607140001  现场实施服务 现场-153         RM0022             气缸     380.00               2.0833                4.17               1583.33\nSO202607140001  现场实施服务 现场-153         RM0023           气动夹爪     620.00               1.0417                2.08               1291.67\nSO202607140001  现场实施服务 现场-153         RM0004          45#圆钢       7.20               3.3125                6.63                 47.70\nSO202607140001  现场实施服务 现场-153         RM0005        精密内六角螺栓       0.85               8.8333               17.67                 15.02\n```\n\n\n请遵循系统设定的主技能规则口径，依据上述执行结果，用通俗易懂的语言给业务用户一份最终 Markdown 总结：\n1. 屏蔽所有技术细节（SQL、表名、代码、字段名一律不出现）；\n2. 若包含多个执行单元，先分单元给出核心结论，再进行整体综合分析与建议；\n3. 若某单元无有效结果或执行失败，如实简要说明，不要编造数据；\n4. 【数据一律表格化】凡是指标、数值、排行、对比、分类汇总、明细清单这类数据，一律用 Markdown 表格呈现，不要写成大段文字或纯项目符号；表格必须有