purchase price.\n        #    The rule "cost set to 0" for no-BOM products seems specific to this logic context (perhaps ignoring overheads or assuming direct pass-through?). However, `erp_material.standard_cost` exists.\n        #    Let\'s follow the explicit rule: "If no BOM, cost = 0". This applies to the *product* being sold.\n        #    So, for each line item:\n        #       1. Find the Material ID corresponding to the product code/name.\n        #       2. Check if this Material has an active BOM (erp_bom where material_id = X and status=2).\n        #       3. If yes, calculate Total Unit Cost = Sum(Child_Material_Standard_Cost * Qty_Per / Base_Qty ... wait, simpler: use plan_cost or rollup).\n        #          The rule says "order quantity multiplied by unit material total cost".\n        #          How to get "unit material total cost"? \n        #          Option A: Use `erp_work_order.plan_cost`? No, that\'s per work order.\n        #          Option B: Calculate from BOM. Unit Cost = SUM(Child.Material.StandardCost * Child.QtyPer / Bom.BaseQty).\n        #          Option C: If no BOM, Cost = 0.\n        \n        # Let\'s refine the data retrieval steps.\n        \n        items = [\n            {"name": "激光测距仪", "code_hint": "激光-215", "qty": 10},\n            {"name": "PU气动软管", "code_hint": "PU-804", "qty": 10},\n            {"name": "码垛机器人", "code_hint": "码垛-418", "qty": 10}\n        ]\n        \n        results = []\n        \n        for item in items:\n            hint = item[\'code_hint\']\n            qty = item[\'qty\']\n            \n            # Search in erp_product first for sales info\n            sql_prod = """\n            SELECT id, product_code, product_name, sale_price \n            FROM nova_erp.erp_product \n            WHERE (product_code LIKE %s OR product_name LIKE %s) AND is_deleted = 0\n            LIMIT 1\n            """\n            # Try matching code hint or name\n            cursor.execute(sql_prod, (f\'%{hint}%\', 